#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Algorithm:3 of
msgid ""
"The three per-segment methods are the API the development tooling drives "
"for its single-page tests. What differs from a naive chaining is *how* "
"they compose, not what they return: the native per-segment API starts "
"from text blocks, so this shim redoes the extraction and filtering chain "
"before deserializing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Algorithm.classify_pages:1 of
msgid ""
"Classifies **a whole document**: which of the format's page classes each "
"page belongs to, `None` for a page the format claims none of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Algorithm.classify_pages:4 of
msgid ""
"Takes the list of `page.get_text(\"dict\")` dicts, in document order, and"
" numbers them from one accordingly. It has to be the whole document and "
"not one page at a time, because a format may supply a finalizer that "
"rewrites the raw per-page answers looking at all of them together — "
"\"every page after the holdings header is holdings\" is the shape of it. "
"A page classified in isolation would then get a different answer from the"
" same page classified in its document, and the isolated one is the wrong "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Algorithm.load:1 of
msgid ""
"**A divergence absorbed here:** the third argument is accepted and "
"ignored. It used to be the list of known formats, which the caller had to"
" fetch and pass; the native loader reads it from the repository itself, "
"so passing it adds nothing — but existing callers still do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Algorithm.page_classes:1 of
msgid "The page classes the schedule visits, in schedule order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.PdfBlock:3 of
msgid "# Why the metadata is a live Python dict, not the native map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.PdfBlock:5 of
msgid ""
"Author code **mutates the metadata in place**: `block.metadata[\"fund\"] "
"= …`. Were the getter to build a fresh dictionary on each read, that line"
" would write into a throwaway object and the change would vanish without "
"an error — the worst way to diverge. The dictionary is therefore **the** "
"container of the metadata, created once at construction and always handed"
" back the same. The native map is derived from it when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Pipeline:3 of
msgid "# A container, not an engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Pipeline:5 of
msgid ""
"This shim does one thing: be the value an author module puts in its "
"pipelines, from which the loader reads the three segments. The loader "
"reads them **by shape** — three attributes, each a callable or an "
"iterable of callables — so that is exactly the contract this type must "
"satisfy, and all it exposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Pipeline:10 of
msgid ""
"Each segment is normalised to a list at construction: nothing becomes an "
"empty list, a single callable a list of one, an iterable is materialised."
" The loader then need not tell the three cases apart, and the order of "
"the pipes is the one the author wrote."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.Pipeline.complete:1 of
msgid "True when all three segments hold at least one pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.TextBlock:3 of
msgid ""
"Not frozen: author code rewrites the content of an already-built block. "
"Equality and hashing are therefore written by hand rather than derived — "
"PyO3 grants hashing only to a frozen class — with the usual caveat of a "
"mutable hashable object: mutating one while it sits in a set makes it "
"unfindable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.core.TextBlock:8 of
msgid ""
"The metadata is a live Python dict for the same reason as [`PyPdfBlock`];"
" see its documentation."
msgstr ""

